PART II — Mid-Term Memory Module (MTMM)
1. Purpose
MTMM is the system’s session memory — holds the compressed record of the current conversation. Where STMM holds only the active processing window (last 2 exchanges), MTMM holds the entire session history in compressed form.
Retention Policy:
MTMM persists for the duration of a session. At session end (or during REM processing), the MemoryConsolidationEngine evaluates MTMM contents for LTMM promotion. Content that doesn’t meet promotion criteria is either archived or discarded.
